M3.1: E820 capture in stage 2 + boot memory ABI + kernel map print

- stage2.s: int 15h E820 ('SMAP') capture while interrupts are still
  on and the BIOS is still alive - deliberately the LAST BIOS data
  call of the boot, made right after the A20 phase. Entries (24-byte
  ACPI layout) land at 0x608 with a u64 count at 0x600, 32 max; empty
  map or garbage ECX fails the boot at the 'X' phase. New phase
  sensor 'M' (sequence is now 1ajULMPK).
- docs/disk-layout.md: the handoff is now a normative ABI table
  (count at 0x600, entries 0x608, 24 B stride); the pointer/struct
  form moves into the image header when that lands.
- mem.c: kernel reads the fixed addresses and prints every entry
  over serial. The page allocator will consume exactly this table.

Evidence (QEMU, 128 MiB): 7 entries, textbook layout - low RAM at
0x0-0x9FC00, ISA/BIOS holes reserved, the big usable run
0x100000-0x7FE0000, EBDA + PCI hole + PCI-E config above. Kernel and
scheduler untouched and green (reports=6 switches=237).
